module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulExtStalk
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulQuotientStalk
public import StacksFrontier.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorPower.HomBaseChange

/-!
# The Ext sheaves of a Koszul-regular quotient at a stalk, as exterior powers of a dual

Let `O♯` be a sheaf of commutative rings on a space, let `φ : (O♯)ʳ ⟶ O♯` generate a sheaf of
ideals, and let `K` be a Koszul complex resolving the quotient `O_X = O♯/𝓘`. Write `S` for the
quotient `O_x ⧸ J_x` of the stalk of `O♯` by the ideal generated by the germs of the generators,
which is a commutative ring. At every point `x`,

`Ext^m_{O♯}(O_X, O_X)_x  ≅  ⋀ᵐ_S(Hom_S(Sʳ, S))`,

the `m`-th exterior power, **over `S`**, of the dual of a free module of rank `r`. In degree one
this reads `Ext^1_x ≅ Hom_S(Sʳ, S)`, so the right-hand side above is the `m`-th exterior power of
the degree-one answer — which is the content of Stacks 0BQY, at a stalk.

This is the composite of three identifications already available: the stalk of the Ext sheaf as
the `O_x`-linear maps out of the stalk of an exterior power; the stalk of the quotient as the
quotient ring `S`; and the base-change identification of `O_x`-linear maps into `S` with
`S`-linear functionals, under which the duality pairing of exterior powers becomes available and
is bijective because `Sʳ` is free of finite rank over `S`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.extStalkDualEquiv`: the identification displayed above.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.ext1StalkDualEquiv`: its degree-one case.

## Implementation notes

**The composite is an equivalence of types, not a linear equivalence.** The three factors are
linear over different rings: the first two over the stalk `O_x` of the structure sheaf, the third
over the quotient `S`. A module over `S` is not automatically a module over `O_x` in Mathlib —
that requires `Module.compHom` or a scalar tower, neither of which is an instance here — so the
factors cannot be composed with `≪≫ₗ`. They are composed as equivalences of types instead, which
is what a bijectivity statement needs; each factor retains its own linearity and can be used
separately where that is wanted.

This is not a defect to be repaired. To strengthen the composite to a linear
equivalence one must first equip the exterior power over `S` with an `O_x`-action, and the only ways
to do that are `Module.compHom` or a scalar tower, neither of which is an instance here; the
strengthening would therefore add structure that nothing downstream uses, since what consumes
this is a bijectivity statement.

**What this does not yet do.** Comparing the right-hand side with the stalk of the *sheaf*
exterior power `⋀ᵐ_{O_X}(Ext^1)` needs the exterior power over `S` to be formed on the stalk of
`Ext^1` as an `S`-module, which in turn needs the stalk of the quotient *ring sheaf* to be
identified with `S` as a **ring** and not only as an `O_x`-module. The identification available
here, `Stacks.RegularSequence.quotientStalkEquiv`, is the module-level one; the ring-level
statement is a separate matter, since it asks that the multiplications agree and is proved from
the first isomorphism theorem for rings rather than for modules.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry HomologicalComplex Stacks.ChainComplex

universe u

namespace Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData

open Stacks.SheafOfModules Stacks.SheafOfModules.SheafHomStalk Stacks.RegularSequence

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {X : TopCat.{u}} (Rc : TopCat.Sheaf CommRingCat.{u} X)
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(Opens.grothendieckTopology X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  {r : ℕ}
  {A : SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X)
    (koszulFreeSheaf Rc r)}
  {φ : koszulFreeSheaf Rc r ⟶
    SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)}

/-- **The Ext sheaves of a Koszul-regular quotient at a stalk are exterior powers of a dual.**
At a point `x`, writing `S` for the quotient of the stalk of `O♯` by the ideal generated by the
germs of the generators, the stalk of `Ext^m_{O♯}(O_X, O_X)` is the `m`-th exterior power over `S`
of the dual of the free `S`-module of rank `r`.

The composite is of the stalk identification of the Ext sheaf, the identification of the stalk of
the quotient with `S`, and the base-change identification of `O_x`-linear maps into `S` with
`S`-linear functionals on the exterior power over `S`. -/
def extStalkDualEquiv (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) [QuasiIso K.augmentation] (m : ℕ)
    (x : X) :
    modStalk
        (derivedSheafExt Rc
          (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
            ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
              (quotient Rc (φ := φ))))
          (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
            ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
              (quotient Rc (φ := φ)))) ((m : ℕ) : ℤ)) x ≃
      ⋀[↑(ringStalk Rc x) ⧸ stalkGermIdeal Rc φ x]^m
        (Module.Dual (↑(ringStalk Rc x) ⧸ stalkGermIdeal Rc φ x)
          (Fin r → (↑(ringStalk Rc x) ⧸ stalkGermIdeal Rc φ x))) :=
  ((extStalkEquiv Rc K m x).toEquiv.trans
    (LinearEquiv.arrowCongr (LinearEquiv.refl (ringStalk Rc x) _)
      (quotientStalkEquiv Rc φ x).symm).toEquiv).trans
    (exteriorPower.exteriorDualFreeBaseChangeEquiv ↑(ringStalk Rc x)
      (↑(ringStalk Rc x) ⧸ stalkGermIdeal Rc φ x) (Fin r) m).toEquiv.symm

/-- **The first Ext sheaf at a stalk is the dual of a free module of rank `r` over the quotient
ring.** This is `extStalkDualEquiv` in degree one, with the first exterior power of a module
identified with the module itself. So the stalk of `Ext^1` is free of rank `r` over the quotient
ring, and the target of `extStalkDualEquiv` is the `m`-th exterior power of it. -/
def ext1StalkDualEquiv (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) [QuasiIso K.augmentation] (x : X) :
    modStalk
        (derivedSheafExt Rc
          (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
            ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
              (quotient Rc (φ := φ))))
          (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
            ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
              (quotient Rc (φ := φ)))) ((1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) x ≃
      Module.Dual (↑(ringStalk Rc x) ⧸ stalkGermIdeal Rc φ x)
        (Fin r → (↑(ringStalk Rc x) ⧸ stalkGermIdeal Rc φ x)) :=
  (extStalkDualEquiv Rc K 1 x).trans
    (exteriorPower.oneEquiv (↑(ringStalk Rc x) ⧸ stalkGermIdeal Rc φ x)
      (Module.Dual (↑(ringStalk Rc x) ⧸ stalkGermIdeal Rc φ x)
        (Fin r → (↑(ringStalk Rc x) ⧸ stalkGermIdeal Rc φ x)))).toEquiv

end Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData

end
